  "entry": "code/phastDNA_gui.py",
  "notes": "Found in a public repository and run by a computer-use agent (batch public-1). A form-based front end to phastDNA that builds the command line to train a fastDNA host classifier from host and phage genome folders, with Bayesian search over hyperparameter ranges, or to predict hosts for new virus FASTA files with a trained classifier, and then shows the run as a task page with a progress stepper, run details and console. Data used in the run: synthetic. tree.json is the workflow the agent did and a second agent replayed; run.json says how.",
